{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And if you will not listen, etc.</b> They were cunning also in this, that they did not say that if they would not do so, then behold they would wage war against them and become avengers of vengeance against them. Therefore they said <b>but if they will not listen</b>, etc. — they will take their daughter and go on their way, and there are no avengers of vengeance here. They were also cunning in this, to show a certain insistence in the matter — that they would not remain dwelling there with them. For otherwise, if they did not express any feeling about the matter, the thoughtful person would suspect cunning in the matter, since the matter was indeed disgraceful according to the truth, as Scripture says: ״וְכֵן לֹא יֵעָשֶׂה״ — even among the nations. Therefore they revealed a certain insistence, and the matter was understood by them in the proper way, for after they would be circumcised it is obvious that there would be a strong bond between them — peace and friendship. And therefore you will find that Shechem and Hamor said to the men of their city: ״הָאֲנָשִׁים הָאֵלֶּה שְׁלֵמִים הֵם״ etc. (Genesis 34:21) — meaning, they sensed from them that there was no cunning in the matter." "<b>Further,</b> it intends in His saying <b>and we will take our daughter</b>: they intended to stir the heart of Hamor and Shechem to hasten to act, for when they see that they are taking the daughter away from him, he will hasten to act, and they will take the vengeance of righteousness from the seed of evildoers."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:58.187432741Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}